## Paste‑ready recipes

### A) Research answer (short, safe, sourced)
```text
&lt;role&gt;You are a careful analyst for {{AUDIENCE}}.&lt;/role&gt;
&lt;task&gt;{{GOAL}} within {{SCOPE}} using the &lt;context&gt;.&lt;/task&gt;
&lt;context&gt;{{DIGEST + key quotes}}&lt;/context&gt;
&lt;process step_back=&quot;ON&quot; skeleton=&quot;ON&quot;/&gt;
&lt;verification policy=&quot;CoVe+CRITIC&quot; tools=&quot;[web,calculator]&quot;/&gt;
&lt;output_format&gt;ONLY: &lt;principles/&gt;&lt;plan/&gt;&lt;skeleton/&gt;&lt;citations/&gt;&lt;final/&gt;&lt;/output_format&gt;
&lt;warning&gt;No PII; if facts unstable, browse and cite before final.&lt;/warning&gt;
```

### B) Brainstorming (fast and diverse)
```text
Goal: Generate 12 ideas for {{TOPIC}} for {{AUDIENCE}}.
Rules: Avoid clichés; vary by channel/time/cost; 1‑line each.
Process: Step‑Back first (3 bullets), then the table.
Output: Table [Idea | Why it works | Next step].
```

### C) RAG discipline
```text
Decide {retrieve|skip}. If retrieve: emit 3 queries, rate passages, cite top 3.
If low confidence, re‑query (CRAG). Then draft → verify → finalize.
Return ONLY: &lt;queries/&gt;&lt;citations/&gt;&lt;final/&gt;.
```

### D) Two‑model critique (cheap win)
```text
Model A: produce draft to schema.
Model B: critique against SUCCESS_CRITERIA; propose fixes.
Model A: revise + short changelog.
```

